{title: Since Jesus Came into My Heart}
{artist: Rufus H. McDaniel / Charles H. Gabriel}
{genre: Gospel}
{flow: Opening}
{style: Traditional}
{key: G}
{key_original: A}
{tempo: 88}
{time: 4/4}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
What a [G]wonderful change in my life has been wrought
Since Jesus came into my [D7]heart
I have [G]light in my soul for which long I had sought
Since Jesus came into my [D7]heart[G]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[G]Since Jesus came into my [C]heart
Since Jesus came into my [G]heart
Floods of [G]joy o'er my soul like the sea billows [D7]roll
Since Jesus came into my [G]heart
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
I have [G]ceased from my wandering and going astray
Since Jesus came into my [D7]heart
And my [G]sins which were many are all washed away
Since Jesus came into my [D7]heart[G]
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
I'm pos[G]sessed of a hope that is steadfast and sure
Since Jesus came into my [D7]heart
And no [G]dark clouds of doubt now my pathway obscure
Since Jesus came into my [D7]heart[G]
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}
